"Jin is bonded to Tianlan, the land spirit; beasts see him as consort to the Earth itself."
"Many sapient Spirit Beasts call Jin 'Emperor', though he sees himself as just Fa Ram's owner."
"Jin and Tianlan deepen their bond through call-and-response music on banjo and pipa."
"Jin can enter the Spirit Realm with Tianlan, using his Qi like roots to brace tunnels."
"Jin's true power is far beyond his reputation; even elder fox cultivators cannot sense its depth."
"At rest, Jin's Qi reaches farther than anyone near him can sense."
"Jin feels the moment family or close friends break through in cultivation."
"Jin senses the exact makeup and hidden flaws of any metal he touches."
"Jin can hold his breath underwater for six hours using Qi."
"Jin once punched Zang Li all the way from Verdant Hill to the Yellow Rock Plateau."
"Jin's Qi-flooded shovel swing hits with mountain-leveling force."
"Jin can fuse his Qi with the ground to tunnel fast or fling up great chunks of earth."
"Jin can ground lightning into the earth, using his shovel like a lightning rod."
"Jin's Path of Shennong has techniques like Break the Rocks, Fell the Trees and Divert the Waters."
"Break the Rocks needs a charge-up and a chant to the Great Ancestor Shennong; it broke Huian's ribs."
"Jin invents techniques mid-fight, like Rooster Tail Broom, which swept away a cloud of poison dust."
"Channeling Tianlan's power without her once cracked Jin's arms like stone, a Spiritual wound."
"Jin secretly killed a demon infiltrator inside the Shrouded Mountain Sect."
"The Grand Ravine Sect suspects Jin is heir to the spirits Tianlan or Xiaoshi."
"Later this year Jin repairs a Dragon Vein, leaving the region's Qi richer than before."
"In time Jin will be hailed as the Herald of the Earth."
